{"t_ms": 682328, "conversation_id": "v2llm_streaming_retrieve_s028", "turn_id": 1, "actor": "system", "event_type": "retrieval_result", "payload": {"passages": ["Parking Policy\n\nGrand Horizon Hotel & Suites\n\nOn-site parking is available for hotel guests at a charge of \u20b9200 per vehicle per day. Parking spaces are allocated on a first-come, first-served basis and cannot be reserved in advance. Guests are requested to lock their vehicles and avoid leaving valuable belongings inside parked cars.", "Vegetarian & Vegan Options\n\nGrand Horizon Hotel & Suites\n\nThe hotel offers a variety of vegetarian and vegan dishes across all dining outlets. Guests can choose from salads, soups, plant-based curries, pasta, rice bowls, and dairy-free desserts. Customized vegan meals can also be prepared upon request. Please inform the restaurant staff of your dietary preferences before ordering.", "# corpus/ \u2014 Hotel Documents\n\n**Owner: Lakshya**\n\n## What this folder is\n\nThe hotel's documents live here: the knowledge the assistant answers from. About 60 short \ndocuments covering things like pool and gym hours, check-in and check-out rules, menus, and \npolicies.\n\n## How to fill it\n\nSee the full instructions in `retrieval/README.md` (Step 1). In short:\n- Write ~60 short documents, one topic per file, as `.txt` or `.md`.\n- Make them realistic and varied.\n- Deliberately plant a few contradictions (e.g. one doc says the pool closes at 10 PM, \n  another says 9 PM) and keep a note of which ones, for a later experiment.\n\nThe index-building script reads every file in this folder, so anything you put here becomes \npart of the searchable knowledge.\n"], "scores": [1.0421340465545654, 1.0440183877944946, 1.060660719871521], "filenames": ["60_parking_v2.txt", "29_vegan_menu.txt", "README.md"], "timing_policy": "sentence_end", "timing_trigger": "sentence_end", "user_end_known_at_finish": true, "launch_offset_ms_vs_user_end": 88, "overlap_with_speech_ms": 0, "forecast_invalidated": false}}
